Hi Peter,

I have an idea for a possible work-around. Are you able to use conda <https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/> on your cluster?

If so, there is a conda package for R with devtools installed <https://anaconda.org/conda-forge/r-devtools>.

You could create a conda environment like this: conda create -n devtools -c conda-forge r-devtools

